      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{60a61b373332241d8a817fb7|full_name}: VRC TOS, Section 12, part d states:  \"post, upload, or distribute any User Content or other content that is unlawful, defamatory, libelous, inaccurate, or that a reasonable person could deem to be objectionable, profane, indecent, pornographic, harassing, threatening, embarrassing, hateful, or otherwise inappropriate;\"\nKeyword to pay attention to is 'pornographic', which NSFW does fall under.  What you could argue is that the behavior itself does not qualify as content, and therefore isn't against the rules, but the avatars/worlds themselves are.  The thing is these tags are specifically for uploaded content, and having tags for something that isn't allowed anymore does not make any sense.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
