  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-11-30T00:01:24.566Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Users new to VRChat often believe the misconception that NSFW is allowed under certain circumstances.  Usually the explanation is either                                \n1.) That NSFW is okay as long as it is marked on upload                               \nor that                                  \n2.) It is okay in Private Instances only.         Obviously, neither is true.  It would do no harm to delete the UI buttons from the Canvas on upload.  It would help a tiny bit to clear up misconceptions.  Unless there is some other crucial element as to why this is still included in the VRCSDK, this should be done...it LITERALLYY takes me like 10 seconds.  I have a video of me doing it. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vm96ZhG9sY0                           \n                                           \nThe existing \"content_sex\" (the tag that deals with NSFW) tag needs to be completely removed from the API (or whatever thingy deals wit that).  If anyone were to search worlds w \"tag:content_sex\" on the VRChat website, it lists every world with that tag.  Those worlds that list upon search did make it past labs, but some are very sussssy if you know what I mean.  It just gives rulebreakers another avenue to network.  Feeds the misconception bleh/.",
